## Structure

```
cmd/
└── main.go                  ← entry point, sets up router

internal/
├── config/config.go           ← reads env
├── middleware/                 ← auth, rate limiting
├── errors/app_error.go         ← error types and helpers
├── shared/                     ← database, cache, health
│   ├── database/
│   ├── cache/
│   └── health/
└── <module>/
    ├── model.go             ← GORM model or plain struct
    ├── repository.go        ← data access (interface + impl)
    ├── service.go           ← business logic
    ├── handler.go           ← Gin handler functions
    ├── dto.go               ← request/response DTOs
    └── routes.go            ← route registration
```

Call direction: `routes` constructs `repository → service → handler`, once per module. A layer only ever talks to the one directly below it.

